From c3724f6270a2019d3da9d053fe8d668a5843e340 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 21:01:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] WIP qsa3: the packed-block WMMA sparse-attention path for
 QSA

Squashed theme commit (5 originals): packed-block WMMA prefill for the QSA
sparse attention; support for every KV cache type (not just the native pair);
the bitmap counting sort in qsa3_rows_kernel (441 -> 25.5 ms); the fused pack
into one launcher pass; and the COMPILE-time gate (LLAMA_QSA3_ENABLE, default 1,
which replaced the rocprofiler-register-racy env gate).

Ported to RDNA4 (2026-09-21, gfx1201): one arch-selected fragment shim
(gfx12 8-half "two runs of four" A/B + accumulator m = 8*hi + e; gfx11 keeps
the 16-half full row and m = 2*e + hi), the F16 _gfx12 builtin, and
ggml_cuda_flash_attn_qsa3_supported() extended to RDNA4.  The gfx11 path is a
compile-time #if, so it is byte-identical.  gfx1201: +7.6/+11.5/+10.4 % prefill
at pp4096/16384/32768 (same build, LLAMA_QSA3_ENABLE 1 vs 0).

Also add the first test-backend-ops coverage that reaches this kernel (the
existing FLASH_ATTN_QSA cases never attach src[7]/src[8], so the packed-block
WMMA path had no oracle on any arch): three packed cases plus the same shape on
the VEC path.  26/26 on gfx1201; qsa3 ~4.2e-8 NMSE vs VEC ~4e-9 (f16 floor).
